Aim

To integrate Jenkins with Docker and build Docker images automatically using Jenkins pipeline.

Theory (Short)

Jenkins is used to automate software builds and deployments.
Docker is used to containerize applications.
Jenkins can execute Docker commands to build and run containers automatically, enabling CI/CD automation.

Steps
Step 1: Install Docker Plugin in Jenkins

Go to:

Manage Jenkins → Plugins

Install:

Docker plugin
Docker Pipeline plugin

Restart Jenkins.

Step 2: Install Docker on System

Check:

docker --version
Step 3: Push Project to GitHub
git init
git add .
git commit -m "Docker Jenkins Integration"
git remote add origin https://github.com/username/lab19.git
git push -u origin main
Step 4: Create Dockerfile
FROM openjdk:17
COPY . /app
WORKDIR /app
RUN javac Hello.java
CMD ["java", "Hello"]
Step 5: Create Jenkinsfile
pipeline {
    agent any

    stages {

        stage('Checkout') {
            steps {
                git 'https://github.com/username/lab19.git'
            }
        }

        stage('Build Docker Image') {
            steps {
                bat 'docker build -t hello-jenkins .'
            }
        }

        stage('Run Container') {
            steps {
                bat 'docker run hello-jenkins'
            }
        }
    }
}
